  RWAOfferingPool hardening
    collateral: one eBL backs one live offering
      ✔ refuses a second offering on an eBL that already backs a live one (59ms)
      ✔ frees the eBL when an unsubscribed offering is cancelled, so it can be offered again (55ms)
      ✔ releases the pledge when an offering is repaid, so the eBL can move again (61ms)
      ✔ still settles when the registry owner already released the pledge, and reports it (62ms)
      ✔ stops selling shares once the eBL is no longer pledged to the pool (51ms)
    pricing bounds
      ✔ never lets the oracle price an offering above its target redemption value (50ms)
      ✔ REPRICE_DOWN has to lower the price (53ms)
      ✔ allows a recovery: an OPEN action may raise a repriced offering again, up to the target (55ms)
      ✔ rejects an out-of-range risk level at the oracle and a zero pool (49ms)
    settlement
      ✔ refuses proofs and settlement for an offering nobody subscribed to (52ms)
      ✔ lets only the owner correct a mistaken importer payment, and keeps the audit trail (63ms)
      ✔ validates a correction (54ms)
      ✔ records the departure proof and the oracle / token wiring in the event log (47ms)
    cancelOffering
      ✔ is owner-only and needs an existing offering (41ms)
      ✔ cannot cancel an offering that already has subscribers (39ms)
      ✔ works from Open, Repriced and Paused, also during a global emergency stop (71ms)
      ✔ rejects a second cancel and any state that is not cancellable (53ms)
    documented limitation
      ✔ subscribe records an amount owed but holds no funds (no payment leg yet) (40ms)

